WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.387
What a working team does.

2
00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:09.325
Put a root span on every request at the edge of your service, and pass the trace id into every log record and eval result.

3
00:00:09.605 --> 00:00:15.771
Record the fields above on every model and tool call, with prompt versions as a first-class attribute.

4
00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:21.299
Keep content off spans by default, and settle your content policy before you turn it on.

5
00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:25.248
Pick one span type as the source of truth for tokens and cost.

6
00:00:25.528 --> 00:00:30.115
Pin your instrumentation versions, because the conventions are still in development.

7
00:00:30.395 --> 00:00:40.848
Then use the traces: the next two lessons turn them into logs you can keep safely, and into dashboards, alerts, and online evals that tell you when the system needs a person.
